      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "For most homeowners in Utah, the average cost of a full roof replacement ranges between $8,500 and $25,000, with the typical single-family home with standard architectural asphalt shingles averaging around $11,000 to $14,800\n\n.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "between $8,500 and $25,000"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Your final bill depends heavily on your home's total square footage, the slope (pitch) of your roof, and the specific materials you choose."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Cost Estimates by Home Size"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Most roofing contractors in Utah base their baseline pricing on standard architectural shingles, which are heavily favored for their ability to withstand the state's extreme temperature swings and high-wind storms:",
        "reference_indexes": [
          2,
          3
        ]
      },
